WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:06.400
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:34.430
<b>Tsurumi Relay Station</b>

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:34.430
<b>Section 9 > Section 10</b>

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.080
<i>The enthusiasm of everyone who's
rushed here to Tsurumi Relay Station</i>

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.680
<i>after Fujioka's Section 9 comeback
has reached its peak.</i>

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>Everyone's excited to see how
anchor and first-year Minami will run.</i>

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.220
<i>Rikudo captain Fujioka Kazuma.</i>

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:26.080
<i>The record-breaking way
he runs is absolute perfection.</i>

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.230
<i>The undisputed champion of four
years demonstrates his full strength</i>

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.390
<i>as he hands off his team's sash.</i>

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.430
<b>Rikudo/Fujioka Fourth-Year 
>>> Minami First-Year</b>

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.950
<i>His time is...</i>

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.430
<b>Section 9 New Section Record</b>

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.910
<i>1:09:00!</i>

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.560
<i>Finishing in exactly 1:09:00,
he sets a new section record!</i>

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.400
<i>With his new Section 9 record,
he adorns himself with excellence.</i>

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.110
Congratulations. You crushed the competition.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.120
You don't mean that.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.130
You were strong and steady today.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.290
I could never catch up.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.000
But Kurahara might.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.670
Kiyose.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.090
How far are we meant to go?

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.810
<i>Motorcycle cam here!</i>

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.040
<i>Does Kurahara have no limits?</i>

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.770
Kansei Kurahara Kakeru First-Year

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>He appears to be accelerating
in the final stages of the section!</i>

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.900
Is there even a finish line that lies ahead?

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.210
But you can't quit.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:39.770
Right?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.250
Have fun.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.270
He'll become even stronger.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:58.610
Fujioka awakens Kakeru,
and Kakeru spurs on Fujioka.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.360
<i>But what about me?</i>

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.950
<b><i>Run With The Wind</i></b>

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.820
<i>Daiwa crosses the relay station.</i>

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.960
<i>Has the team returned to form?</i>

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.820
<i>The next team to enter
the relay station is Kita Kanto.</i>

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.110
<b>Marunouchi North</b>

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:49.440
<i>Kita Kanto's Higure climbs three ranks.</i>

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.910
<i>They'll surely be back next year.</i>

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.130
Is Kakeru not there yet?

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.130
It's way too soon.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.570
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.340
Kansei's coming next!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.800
Wasn't Kansei part of the simultaneous start?

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.750
With ten minutes to make 
up on the second half...

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.110
Haiji.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:12.230
I shouldn't be saying this
before it's over, but I had fun.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:14.690
Did you?

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.080
Me, too.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:23.070
So as long as you make 
it back in one piece...

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.530
Just kidding.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.740
Go ahead. Run as much as you'd like.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.230
I will.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.800
<i>I've experienced a runner's high before,</i>

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.720
<i>but this is different.</i>

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.180
<i>I feel powerless.</i>

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.180
<i>I feel comfortable as though
I'm dreaming, but also anxious.</i>

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.010
<i>My body moves on its own,</i>

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.110
<i>leaving my consciousness behind.</i>

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.110
<i>Haiji!</i>

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:14.080
<i>That night, when you passed
before my eyes, I had a thought.</i>

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.670
<i>“That's my dream right there.”</i>

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.620
<i>“It's taken shape, and it's running.”</i>

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.690
<i>You made such an impact, I wanted to scream.</i>

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:25.090
<i>What I'd been struggling
to achieve was right there.</i>

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:30.600
<i>You are the ideal form I never reached.</i>

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.890
<i>Did you know?</i>

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:38.100
<i>When you run, I see a single
white line of light at your feet,</i>

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:41.520
<i>like a shooting star.</i>

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.700
<b><i>In The Wind</i></b>

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.580
Kakeru!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.320
You did it, Kakeru!

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.550
You did it!

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:09.220
<i>Kurahara Kakeru's time
is an unbelievable 1:08:59!</i>

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.220
<b>Kansei Kurahara Kakeru First-Year</b>

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.220
<b>Section 9 New Section Record</b>

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.180
<i>He's broken the section record!</i>

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:17.150
<i>Kansei's Kurahara Kakeru breaks
Fujioka Kazuma's 1:09:00 record</i>

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.600
<i>a mere eleven minutes later.</i>

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:24.770
<i>The difference is only one second,
but it's the biggest shock of the race.</i>

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.990
<i>Kurahara Kakeru overwrites the section record</i>

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.380
<i>and goes down in Hakone Ekiden history.</i>

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:34.690
<i>This rookie has put the brakes
on the happy ending</i>

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.800
<i>of four-year track champion Fujioka.</i>

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.370
Happy ending?

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.450
It's not over.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.120
Kurahara, could we get a comment?

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.160
Kakeru!

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.300
At least wipe off your sweat, Kakeru!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.510
We need to get there before Haiji!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.970
Hurry, Prince!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.350
Please stop sprinting!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.170
Come on! Run!

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:57.350
I don't want to run anymore!

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.830
<b>Tsurumi Relay Station</b>

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.830
<b>Section 9 > Section 10</b>

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:10.490
<b>Rikudo
Boso
Daiwa
Kitakan
Manaka
Yokohama
Dochido
Kikui
Saikyo
Tokyo Sport
Top 10 Seeded Schools
Akebono
Kansei
Kofu Academy
Nihonbashi Tech
Teito
Jonan Bunka
Eurasia
Shinsei
Kanagawa
Tokyo Academy
OP Student Association</b>

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.860
<i>Here are the overall times
at the end of Section 9.</i>

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:06.480
<i>First place, Rikudo, 9:53:51.</i>

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:10.490
<i>Second place, Boso, 9:55:22.</i>

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:15.490
And Kansei's time is 10:06:27.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.000
Our overall position is 12th.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:26.750
<b>1 Rikudo
2 Boso
3 Daiwa
4 Kitakan
5 Manaka
6 Yokohama
7 Dochido
8 Kikui
9 Saikyo
10 Tokyo Sport
Top 10 Seeded Schools
11 Akebono
12 Kansei
13 Kofu Academy
14 Nihonbashi Tech
15 Teito</b>

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:22.530
To get into the top 10 and earn a seed,

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:27.560
you'll have to finish 1:02
faster than Tokyo Sport.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:33.230
But your target, Tokyo Sport,
is currently running behind you.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.850
Right now, the numbers 
are all we can rely on.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:42.020
Listen closely: At three kilometers,
Tokyo Sport's one kilometer time was 3:05.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.350
You're running at a 3:03 pace.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.190
In other words...

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.070
This painkiller is permitted
in-competition.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.580
It will suppress the pain and inflammation.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:00.730
I can't tell you not to push yourself,
but no matter what happens—

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.540
I have teammates who brought me this far.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.790
I'm prepared.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.100
Guys!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.780
Hana!

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.220
Who's a good boy?

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:29.620
Nira, this is the first time
I've been glad to see you.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.010
How could you say that to him?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.950
Huh? Where's Joji?

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.950
Who's a good boy? You're a good boy.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.950
You're so cute.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.960
He's on his way here with King.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.340
Oh, I see. I hope he gets here soon.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.530
Joji, too.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:47.580
Uh, yeah. And King.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.170
Hana, I have a question for you. Do you mind?

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.680
Tokyo Sport's pace might be slowing.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:55.930
I'll check.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.260
What?!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.310
<b>Section 10 10km Point</b>

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.770
Tokyo Sport's pace is slowing.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.690
Keep it up.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.340
<i>Sorry for making unreasonable demands.</i>

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.940
<i>The skies always looked
like this back home, too.</i>

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.030
<i>Always cloudy.</i>

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.460
<b>Kiyose</b>

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.460
Honey.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.680
Not today.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.870
Practice starts on this day every year.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.430
He's him.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.230
I'm me.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.030
Haiji.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.400
Don't lose your head.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.670
<i>I want to run after all.</i>

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.510
<i>I finally understand.</i>

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.140
<i>Whether I run or I don't,
it hurts just the same.</i>

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:31.020
<i>Even if I fail, I want to do what
my heart desires here.</i>

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:40.910
<b>Kansei University
 Track and Field Club</b>

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.370
You're a cursed man.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:52.290
Wherever you are, it always
becomes the course you'll run.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.000
You'll need ten teammates first, though.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:57.010
I'll do it.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.120
I'll create the ultimate team.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.620
<i>Are you watching, dad?</i>

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:09.430
<i>This is the team I met.</i>

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:17.230
<i>Kansei's Kiyose Haiji pulls head
of Yokohama and increases his pace.</i>

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>He's running to pass on the hope
the ten of them built to future generations.</i>

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.260
<i>They are the ultimate team.</i>

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.780
<i>The hope I finally seized.</i>

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.590
<i>I lost hope once.</i>

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.280
<i>I felt betrayed by myself
and the entire world.</i>

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.810
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:44.780
<i>Running returned to me in 
an even more beautiful form.</i>

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.640
<i>Can one man be so blessed?</i>

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.670
<i>I'm happy.</i>

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.520
<i>I could cry.</i>

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.440
<i>I am truly happy.</i>

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:04.910
<i>Even if I can never run again,</i>

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:13.260
<i>I love running!</i>

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:27.010
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.160
<i>The temperature in Otemachi,
Tokyo is 0.4 degrees.</i>

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.690
<i>The snow has stopped,
but the wind continues to blow.</i>

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:39.470
<i>The first runner will be arriving
at the Yomiuri HQ finish line shortly.</i>

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.860
Pain killers?

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.350
Yes, this morning.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.320
Should you be saying that?

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:50.290
Wouldn't you guys rather know?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.490
I knew it. He's sweating too much.

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.500
Now that I look closely,
his expression is stiff, too.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:13:00.120
He won't listen if we try to stop him now.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.780
Tokyo Sport shows no signs
of backing down, either.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.650
Everyone's desperate.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.820
Let's trust him.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.470
Haiji will show us

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:24.700
the ultimate goal we're aiming for.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.250
<i>Deflecting the pressure
from the other schools,</i>

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.350
<i>Once again, Rikudo rises to the top</i>

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.810
Minami! Final spurt!

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.350
<i>of the Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip
College Ekiden Race.</i>

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.080
<i>They've won again.</i>

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.000
<i>This is the power of a champion.</i>

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.760
<i>They gather around Captain
Fujioka to celebrate their victory.</i>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Boso</b>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Daiwa</b>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Kitakan</b>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Manaka</b>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Kansei</b>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
<b>Yokohama</b>

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:06.150
<i>Haiji, Yuki calculated an estimate.</i>

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:10.070
<i>At this rate, you'll be six seconds
short of Tokyo Sport and tenth place.</i>

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.790
<i>Three kilometers remain.</i>

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:14.450
<i>The rest is up to you.</i>

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:29.490
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.870
<b>Kansei</b>

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:35.870
<i>It's Kansei Uni.</i>

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:40.540
<i>Fifth to arrive in Otemachi
is first-timer Kansei University.</i>

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:24.090
<i>They've achieved an unprecedented
fifth place finish with only ten members.</i>

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:28.710
<i>They finished last in Section 1, but they 
steadily climbed the ranks until Section 5,</i>

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.540
<i>where they fell behind again
after a shocking loss of speed.</i>

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.800
<i>In today's second half, they were
part of the simultaneous start.</i>

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:40.130
<i>With impressive teamwork and 
a section record, they overcame adversity.</i>

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:42.600
<i>They are a truly miraculous team.</i>

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:50.030
<i>Kansei's participation made 
this an exciting race, indeed.</i>

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:54.990
<i>You asked me once what running is.</i>

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.950
<i>You said you wanted to know what it is.</i>

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:04.320
<i>The answer is you.</i>

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.380
<i>It's you.</i>

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:25.570
<i>Kansei University places 
a remarkable fifth in the second half.</i>

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:30.690
<i>With a time of 5:34:32, they've
completed the Tokyo-Hakone race.</i>

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.190
<b>Tokyo-Hakone</b>

00:17:53.710 --> 00:18:05.020
<b>8 Kikui

00:17:53.710 --> 00:18:05.020
<b>Top 10 Seeded Schools</b>

00:17:53.710 --> 00:18:05.020
<b>11 Tokyo Sport</b>

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.780
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.680
Well? Did you get to see the top?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:13.590
By the time the cherry blossoms bloomed,

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.590
<b>Demolition Notice

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.590
the ten of us gathered
at the dilapidated Chikusei-so,

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.260
which was scheduled to be demolished.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.720
It's exploitative.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:29.560
Just thinking about you working
brings tears to my eyes.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.640
How about you, Musa?
I'm happy to give you advice.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.020
I'm staying in grad school for another year.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:36.090
Thanks for waiting.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:37.860
We brought more drinks.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.980
Hey, fourth-years.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:41.780
We came to say our goodbyes.

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.210
You guys came?

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.490
<i>Everyone's following their own path.</i>

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.750
<b>Land of the Gods</b>

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.750
<b>Steepest in the World</b>

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.750
Let's drink today, Kakeru.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:53.360
Okay.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:57.800
<i>Haiji's begun running a new path, too.</i>

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:01.510
Think it'll work out?

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:04.900
I'm not sure. It is a new team.

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.360
But you'd be coaching a works team, right?

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:09.020
Sounds exciting.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:13.230
Just tell us already. It's been three years.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:17.310
Yeah, it's been long 
enough. Which one was it?

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.610
No way! Was it written on my face?

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.330
Promise me you won't tell anyone!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.150
I promise.

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.760
So, uh... Which is it?

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:30.380
What?

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.080
Which one do you like, Hana?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.900
Which one?

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.670
That's between me and Hana.

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.640
Get him, boys.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:53.130
What are you guys doing?

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:54.850
How's the new team?

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:57.120
It's stronger than back then.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:58.030
Yeah.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:20:59.740
Really?

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:02.990
You can't go back in time.

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:08.730
Just as old records are overwritten,
we keep moving forward.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.500
Sometimes it makes me sad, but that's...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.500
I'm excited for this winter.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.720
Me, too.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.300
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.220
Hey!

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:36.690
It's time! Break's over!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.150
What? Just a little longer.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:43.360
You're fourth-years now.
Pull yourselves together.

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:46.170
That's my favorite thing about her.

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:49.570
Hey, we agreed no shenanigans
until after we graduate.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:51.780
Let's go.

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:53.120
Yes, sir!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.040
The wind is blowing.

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:00.110
And we defy it by running.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.460
Believing the answer we seek lies ahead.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:06.550
What is strength?

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:08.090
What is running?

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.320
What is living?

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.510
It's all beyond the wind.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.310
Hope resides within our hearts.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:19.020
Look. The road is right before your eyes.

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:22.260
So we run again today.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.540
We'll run to the edges of the earth.

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:36.350
Hey, do you like running?
